WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.250
On the road to Damascus, Acts says, a
light from the sky suddenly shone around

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.230
Paul.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:11.200
Today, stimulating part of the brain
can produce religious-seeming states.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.880
And Christians, Hindus and Buddhists
report experiences that support different

5
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:16.970
beliefs.

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.860
So when a Christian says God spoke to her,

7
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.230
can science, philosophy or other
religions show she is wrong?

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.290
In this mission, you'll meet
tests for an experience,

9
00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.690
from the Bible to William James.

10
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.850
Then you'll sort thinkers into 4
ways science and religion relate,

11
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.270
and weigh Hume on miracles.

12
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.310
Your mission: weigh up whether science,
philosophy or other religions could show

13
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.730
a religious experience is mistaken.
